  "kanji": "川",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 川\ntitle: river\njlpt: 5\ntags: [jlpt-n5, grade-1, pictograph, starter]\nstrokes: 3\nradical: 川\nradicalNumber: 47\nonyomi: [セン]\nkunyomi: [かわ]\ndistractors: [山, 水, 州]\n---\n\n# 川 — river\n\n**Strokes:** 3 · **Key (radical):** 川 (no. 47) · **JLPT:** N5 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n川 is a pictograph of a stream: lines of water flowing between banks. The exact reading of the three lines varies\nbetween accounts; the learning point is \"flowing water\".\nThe related 州 (province, state) is explained as land (sandbars, islets) in a river, so it keeps the three flows with extra marks.\nCompare 水 ([水](水.md)), the general word for water, and 巛, an old variant of the river key.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| セン | on | 河川 かせん, 山川 さんせん (literary) |\n| かわ | kun | 川 かわ, [川上](../words/川上.md) かわかみ, 川下 かわしも, 川辺 かわべ |\n| -がわ | kun (voiced) | [小川](../words/小川.md) おがわ, 隅田川 すみだがわ |\n\nIn compounds 川 is often voiced (小川, 隅田川), but not always: 石川 いしかわ.\n\n## Common words\n\n- [小川](../words/小川.md) おがわ — brook\n- [川上](../words/川上.md) かわかみ — upstream\n- 川 かわ — river\n\n## Notes\n\n川 vs 河: 河 is a different character, also read かわ, mostly seen in compounds and names (黄河 こうが, 河川 かせん). Treat 川 as the\neveryday spelling; \"大きい川 = 河\" is not a reliable rule.\n",
